    <DataNode elementId="AT2G31830-MONOMER" textLabel="phosphatidylinositol/ inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT2G31830-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="395" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">5PTase14 has |FRAME: MG+2 Mg&lt;SUP&gt;2+&lt;/SUP&gt;|-dependent inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase activity against |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4,5-bisphosphate| with lower levels of activity against |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYLINOSITOL-345-TRIPHOSPHATE 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate| and the soluble |FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,4,5)-trisphosphate| when its activity is tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; following expression in yeast. In the same assays, it shows no activity against several other membrane-based phosphoinositides (|FRAME: CPD-177 a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate|, |FRAME: CPD-1108 a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4-phosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-5-PHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 5-phosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-34-BISPH a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4-bisphosphate|, or |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-35-BISPH 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,5-bisphosphate|), nor does it show any activity with the soluble tetraphosphate inositol |FRAME: CPD-506 D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,3,4,5)-tetrakisphosphate| |CITS: [15574849]|. Interestingly, in addition to its type II 5PTase domain, this enzyme also has a WD40 domain which is typically associated with protein-protein interactions. 5PTase14 transcripts appear to be expressed at higher levels in seedlings and inflorescence apices than in other organs. In addition, 5PTase14 transcript expression levels appear to decrease slightly in response to a dark treatment |CITS: [15574849]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G31830-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase (type II)" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33276, RXN-20320, RXN-20329, RXN-T9-772" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G31830.2" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G31830" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15574849" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G47510-MONOMER" textLabel="Type IV inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase 11" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q5EAF2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">5PTase11 has phosphatidylinositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase activity against |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4,5-bisphosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-35-BISPH 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,5-bisphosphate|, and |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYLINOSITOL-345-TRIPHOSPHATE 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate| when its activity is tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; following expression in insect cells |CITS: [15181205]|. Meanwhile, under the same experimental conditions, no activity is observed with the monophosphorylated phosphotidyl inositol PI(5)P nor with the soluble |FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,4,5)-trisphosphate| or |FRAME: CPD-506 D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,3,4,5)-tetrakisphosphate| |CITS: [15181205]|. This protein is the smallest of the putative 15 members of the inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase family in Arabidopsis |CITS: [15181205]|. 5PTase11 transcripts appear to be expressed throughout the plant but seem to be present at higher levels in roots than in other organs. In addition, 5PTase11 transcript expression levels appear to increase in response to a treatment with auxin and jasmonic acid |CITS: [15181205]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G47510-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G47510.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q5EAF2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="At5PTase11" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-20332, RXN-20331, RXN-T9-2047" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="3" />
